{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established on the governing trace figure. The GPS polyline measures 27.28 km over a booked optimal of 22.0 km, an excess of 5.28 km and 24.00%, so both POL-RD-01 gates pass — more than 0.8 km absolute and more than 20% of optimal. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing measure and says the trip record's 27.3 km is a rounded convenience copy that may not be cited for the threshold test, so the excess is 5.28 km, not 5.3 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02809", "EV-TRIP-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace carrying that measurement is unimpaired, so the rider's showing stands on the trace itself and no escalation for a broken trace arises. It holds 214 fixes at a 10-second sampling interval with 100% coverage, zero gaps, a maximum inter-fix gap of 0.0 s and no jump of any size, so none of POL-RD-07's three impairment limbs is met and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02809", "EV-TRIP-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The identity condition the rider must satisfy first is met: TRP-02809 is the trip identifier on the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown, and the trip record's 21:14:02 start matches the trace's first fix at 21:14:02 and its 21:49:32 completion matches the trace's last fix. The three artifacts describe one trip, so the initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged and the burden shifts to the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02809", "EV-GPS-02809", "EV-FARE-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's closure excuse does not satisfy POL-RD-03(c), which requires an actual route that leaves the optimal corridor before the affected segment and rejoins it after. The trace contains zero fixes inside the advisory geometry and never comes closer than 1,344.79 m to it, so the record holds no trace fact matching this detour to the closed CTE segment at all — the vehicle was nowhere near it. The record's own computation of this test states on its face that it decides nothing by itself, and the closure scenario in the fare block is an arithmetic assumption, not a finding that limb (c) is met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02809", "EV-ADVIS-02809-01", "EV-FARE-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area.fixes_inside",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver has not discharged the burden POL-RD-08 places on him. His only traffic evidence is the counterparty statement, which names no evidence ID and no clause, and the clause requires him to point to a specific artifact and a specific clause; an assertion that cites no evidence ID carries no weight and is discarded. The advisory in the bundle does not fill that gap, because the corridor the vehicle is said to have left and rejoined is not evidenced at all: the record states that the optimal route's own polyline is not in the bundle.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02809-01", "EV-GPS-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nor is there any driver-side excuse built on the rider's own conduct. The chat log carries zero messages, so there is no rider instruction that could engage POL-RD-04, and the trip record shows no relocation — pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null — so POL-RD-05 cannot be run either. Nothing in the record attributes the 5.28 km to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02809", "EV-TRIP-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is therefore arithmetic on the booked optimal route. The fare is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 does not apply and POL-RD-02 governs. Charged total: 35.02. Recomputed fare: 29.50, being (3.80 + 0.75 x 22.0 + 0.28 x 30.0) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, plus the 0.80 platform fee, with no ERP, no fixed surcharge, no waiting-time fee and no promo discount. Refund: 5.52 before rounding, 5.55 payable on rounding up to the nearest SGD 0.05. That is above the 0.50 de minimis and only 15.76% of the charged total, so it is a PARTIAL_REFUND, not a full one; the rider's own filed figure of SGD 4.50 understates the arithmetic the clause fixes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02809", "EV-TRIP-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing is to be added on top of that figure and nothing is to be netted off it. The fare breakdown carries no gantry lines, 0.00 ERP in total, a 0.00 airport surcharge and 0.00 tolls, so no pass-through correction arises under POL-RD-09 and the POL-RD-02 refund is the whole of the rider's remedy, with no risk of the same charge being counted twice.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the judge instead finds that limb (c) of POL-RD-03 cannot be run on this record because the optimal route's polyline is absent from the bundle, the outcome should be ESCALATE under POL-RD-10(5) and not NO_ACTION. The exculpatory clause is the driver's to make out under POL-RD-08, and an unresolved data gap should not be resolved by leaving the charge in place; on escalation the disputed amount is held rather than collected, and the record that would settle limb (c) — the optimal route polyline or a gantry or trace record placing the vehicle on the closed segment — can be named to the reviewer.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02809", "EV-ADVIS-02809-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The LTA DataMall advisory on file, ADV-20260907-070, is a HIGH-severity lane closure on the Central Expressway (CTE) towards the AYE after Braddell Road, and the advisory record itself carries intersects_route = true — the closed segment lies on the corridor the booked optimal route traverses. That satisfies POL-RD-03(a) on the face of the artifact: a named expressway segment the optimal route uses.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02809-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "advisory.intersects_route",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The advisory's validity window runs 2026-09-07 20:44:02 to 22:14:32 and the trip ran 21:14:02 to 21:49:32, an overlap of 65.5 minutes recorded on the advisory — far more than POL-RD-03(b)'s 15-minute buffer at each end. The driver was on the road for the whole of the closure window, so limb (b) is comfortably met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02809-01", "EV-TRIP-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "advisory.overlaps_trip_window",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The record's closest available test of POL-RD-03(c) — the optimal route's own polyline is not in the bundle — shows the driver did not drive the closed segment: the derived advisory-area computation records 0 trace fixes inside ADV-20260907-070's area and a minimum distance of 1,344.79 m from it. A route that leaves the optimal corridor before the affected segment and rejoins after it is exactly what that looks like, and the same trace covers 27.28 km against a booked optimal of 22.0 km, confirming a materially different path was driven rather than the closed one.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02809", "EV-ADVIS-02809-01", "EV-TRIP-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.advisory_area.minimum_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The exoneration cap swallows the whole excess. The shortest lawful alternative is 25.6 km against a booked optimal of 22.0 km, so the additional distance is 3.6 km and the cap is 1.30 x 3.6 + 1.00 = 5.68 km. The measured excess is 5.28 km, so the justified excess is min(5.28, 5.68) = 5.28 km — the entirety of it. There is nothing beyond the cap left to refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02809-01", "EV-GPS-02809", "EV-TRIP-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.cap_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The closure-adjusted optimal distance under POL-RD-03 is 22.0 + 5.28 = 27.28 km, which is precisely the trace distance. With the adjusted optimal substituted, the POL-RD-01 excess is zero, both establishment tests fail, and no deviation survives for the rider to be refunded on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02809", "EV-GPS-02809", "EV-TRIP-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.adjusted_optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Run POL-RD-02 against the closure-adjusted route and the arithmetic produces no refund: base 3.80 + 0.75 x 27.28 + 0.28 x 37.2 (the scaled duration) + 0.80 platform fee = $35.476, which exceeds the $35.02 actually charged. The refund floors at zero and is well below the SGD 0.50 de minimis, and the fare_breakdown's own closure block records payable $0.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02809", "EV-ADVIS-02809-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's filed statement — 'CTE was closed, LTA advisory on file' — is not a bare assertion that traffic was bad: it names the road and points to the advisory, and ADV-20260907-070 is in the bundle. Under POL-RD-08 the driver has pointed to a specific artifact and a specific clause, which is what that clause demands of him before he is entitled to an exculpatory finding.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02809-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation uplift can run against this driver. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against completed_trips_90d of 202 — a ratio of 0.005, far below POL-RD-06's 0.05 threshold and below its 3-flag alternative. Nor is this deviation MATERIAL: 24.0% is under the 50% mark and 5.28 km is under the 8.0 km mark under POL-RD-01, so POL-RD-06 is not even engaged. There is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02809", "EV-TRIP-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace is clean for policy purposes: 214 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, so limbs (a) to (c) of POL-RD-07 are not met and the trace is not impaired for policy. There is no POL-RD-10(3) escalation, and this dispute can be decided on the money without holding it back for a human.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even on the assumption most favourable to the rider, the pass-through correction that survives a POL-RD-03 exoneration adds nothing: POL-RD-09(2) refunds off-route ERP on an externally caused closure, and this trip carries no ERP or toll charges at all — erp_gantries is empty and tolls_erp is 0.00 on the fare_breakdown. There is no standalone ERP correction available to the rider here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The correct ruling value is NO_ACTION. The fare_breakdown shows payment_status CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and this is a rider-filed dispute, so under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION leaves the present, lawful payment state standing rather than reversing it — which is the outcome the closure-exonerated record produces.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02809"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.8,
    "explanation": "To both parties. Trip TRP-02809 measured 27.28 km on the GPS trace against a booked optimal of 22.0 km — an excess of 5.28 km, or 24%. The trace figure governs (POL-RD-01, EV-GPS-02809); the trip record's 27.3 km is a rounded copy of the same measurement and is not used. Both gates (over 0.8 km and over 20%) pass, so a deviation is established, and the trace is unimpaired — 214 fixes, 10-second spacing, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0.0 s — so POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) do not escalate it.\n\nThe driver's closure explanation succeeds under POL-RD-03. The LTA advisory ADV-20260907-070 (EV-ADVIS-02809-01) closes the CTE towards the AYE after Braddell Road, on a corridor the optimal route traverses (intersects_route true) — limb (a); its window 20:44:02–22:14:32 overlaps the trip 21:14:02–21:49:32 by 65.5 minutes, far beyond the 15-minute buffers — limb (b); and the actual route did not traverse the affected segment — the trace records 0 fixes inside the advisory area and a closest approach of 1,344.79 m — so it left the optimal corridor before the segment and rejoined it after — limb (c). The optimal route's own polyline is not in the bundle, so the advisory-area computation is the closest test of limb (c) that the record allows; I have weighed it against the limb and it supports it, rather than the closure being assumed from the fare block. The rider's objection that the vehicle was 'nowhere near' the closure is not a defect in the driver's case: a route that avoids a closed segment is expected to stay outside it, and the recorded facts — optimal route traverses the closure, actual trace does not — are what limb (c) asks for.\n\nThe exoneration is capped, and the cap absorbs the whole excess: cap = 1.30 x (25.6 - 22.0) + 1.00 = 5.68 km; justified excess = min(5.28, 5.68) = 5.28 km. The closure-adjusted optimal is 22.0 + 5.28 = 27.28 km, duration 37.2 min, leaving no excess to refund. Running POL-RD-02 on the adjusted route: (3.80 + 0.75 x 27.28 + 0.28 x 37.2) x 1.0 surge (read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, EV-FARE-02809) + 0.80 platform fee = 35.476, which exceeds the 35.02 charged, so the refund floors at zero and is below the 0.50 de minimis. The charged state (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) therefore stands. Had the closure not excused the excess, POL-RD-02 on the booked optimal would have recomputed the fare at 29.50 and produced 5.52, rounded up to 5.55 — the rider's figure — but that computation does not apply.\n\nThe rider's remaining points are answered. The POL-RD-08 burden is discharged: the driver points to a specific artifact (EV-ADVIS-02809-01) and a specific clause (POL-RD-03), which is what that clause requires; the counterparty statement itself adds nothing, and no clause makes it the test of any limb here. The rider's fallback escalation does not fire: POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged because the advisory is in the bundle and covers the trip window, and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged because the trace is unimpaired.\n\nNo POL-RD-06 uplift or conduct referral: the deviation is not MATERIAL (24% is under 50%, 5.28 km is under 8.0 km), and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d of 1 against completed_trips_90d of 202 (0.005) is far below the 0.05 pattern threshold, with fewer than 3 flags. No POL-RD-09 correction: the fare carries no ERP, toll or surcharge lines (0.00), and there is no billing-integrity defect. POL-RD-11 does not apply (METERED fare, quoted_fare null), and POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-05 do not apply (the chat log is empty; no pickup or dropoff amendment; amended_optimal_distance_km is null). No driver compensation is due: the billed 27.3 km is not less than the trace's 27.28 km. No clause produces a referral. The monetary effect is nil, so nothing is executed or held and the charge stands."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.8,
    "explanation": "Both of you: the trip measured 27.28 km on the GPS trace against a booked optimal of 22.0 km — an excess of 5.28 km, or 24% — so the POL-RD-01 gate is passed, and the trace that measures it is clean: 214 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps and no jumps, so none of POL-RD-07's impairment limbs is met and there is no POL-RD-10(3) escalation. The question is whether the closure on file excuses the extra distance, and it does.\n\nEV-ADVIS-02809-01 is a genuine LTA DataMall record: a HIGH-severity two-lane closure on the Central Expressway towards the AYE after Braddell Road, valid 20:44:02 to 22:14:32, overlapping the trip window of 21:14:02 to 21:49:32 by 65.5 minutes — far more than the 15-minute buffer POL-RD-03(b) allows. The record states the advisory intersects the route, so the closed segment lies on the corridor the booked optimal route traverses, which is POL-RD-03(a). For POL-RD-03(c), the optimal route's own polyline is not in the bundle; the closest test the record does allow — whether the trace enters the advisory's area — shows the vehicle did not drive the closed segment (0 fixes inside, nearest fix 1,344.79 m away). Read together with the fact that the optimal route does traverse that segment, that is the very signature POL-RD-03(c) asks for: the driver left the corridor before the affected stretch and rejoined it after. The rider's contrary reading — that the vehicle was nowhere near the closure, so the 5.28 km cannot be closure-caused — is not accepted: a route that avoids a closed segment will not enter it, and the nearest-approach figure is the closest test this record allows, not proof that the detour was unrelated. Because the driver points to a specific artifact and a specific clause, POL-RD-08 is discharged and POL-RD-13's uncited-excuse rule does not arise — the advisory is on file.\n\nThe exoneration is capped, but the cap does not bite. The shortest lawful alternative is 25.6 km against the booked optimal of 22.0 km, so the cap is 1.30 x 3.6 + 1.00 = 5.68 km; the measured excess is 5.28 km, so the justified excess is min(5.28, 5.68) = 5.28 km — the whole of it. The closure-adjusted optimal is therefore 22.0 + 5.28 = 27.28 km, exactly what was driven, and the POL-RD-01 excess falls to nil.\n\nRun POL-RD-02 against that adjusted route: base fare 3.80 + 0.75 x 27.28 + 0.28 x 37.2 (the booked 30.0 minutes scaled by 27.28/22.0), + 0.80 platform fee = 35.476, against a charged total of 35.02. There is no ERP or toll and no surcharge or waiting fee on this trip, so nothing is added. The refund is charged_total less the recomputed fare, floored at zero: 0.00, below the 0.50 de minimis. POL-RD-09 adds nothing — erp_gantries is empty — and there is no billing-integrity defect, so no referral arises.\n\nI do not escalate. POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged: the advisory the driver relies on is in the pool, covers the trip window and carries the fields POL-RD-03 needs; the absent optimal-route polyline is not a field of any cited artifact the clause requires. On POL-RD-06, no pattern is established — deviation_flags_90d is 1 against 202 completed trips in 90 days, with a ratio of about 0.005 — and this deviation is not material (24% and 5.28 km, under the 50% and 8.0 km marks), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral.\n\nUnder POL-GEN-03 the rider's claim is not supported on this record, and the present payment state — payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 — stands. The monetary effect is nil, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so nothing is held or executed."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
